 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Inserting into a red-black tree can only create two reds in a row. Deleting is harder: removing a black node shortens some paths, breaking the equal-black rule. This video shows the idea of a double-black node, and the four cases that remove it."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "head"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Red-black trees, part 2"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here are the seven stages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Deleting as in a BST, the easy outcomes, the double-black node, and four cases decided by the sibling."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then one deletion that needs three of the cases in turn, the costs, and an exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[4..=6]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "bst",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: start as in an ordinary BST. If z has at most one child, z itself is removed, and its child, or nil, takes its place. Call that node x."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 7: delete as in a BST"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "st"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "st[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "If z has two children, its successor y moves into z's position and takes z's colour. Then it is y that has really left its old spot, and y's child becomes x."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "st[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So what matters is the colour of the node that really disappeared from its position."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "st[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "track the colour that left, and the node x that replaced it"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "easy",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: if that colour was red, nothing breaks. Black counts are unchanged, and a red node removed cannot create two reds in a row. Done."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 7: when nothing needs fixing"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "st[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "If it was black, every path through x lost one black node. That breaks rule 5, and needs fixing."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "st[4]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Two quick cases: if x is red, colour it black. The missing black is back."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "st"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "db"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "db[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "If x is the root, every path lost one black equally, so the rule still holds. Done."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "db[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "removed red: done · x red: paint it black"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "dbl",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3: otherwise x is black and not the root. Cormen pretends x carries an extra black: it is double black, counting as two. That restores the counts, but breaks the rule that a node is red or black."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 3 of 7: the double-black node"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "db[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The fix moves that extra black up the tree, or rotates it away, by looking at x's sibling, w, and w's children."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "db[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "double black: an extra black to get rid of"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cases",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4: case 1, the sibling w is red. Rotate at the parent and swap the colours of w and the parent. Now x has a black sibling, so one of the other cases applies."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 4 of 7: four cases"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "db"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "cs"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cs[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Case 2, w is black and both its children are black. Take one black off both x and w: w turns red, and the extra black moves up to the parent, which becomes the new x."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cs[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Case 3, w is black, its near child is red and its far child black. Rotate at w and swap colours, so the red child becomes the far one: that is case 4."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cs[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Case 4, w is black and its far child is red. Rotate at the parent, give w the parent's colour, and colour the parent and the far child black. The extra black is absorbed, and the fix ends."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "cs[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Case 2 may climb towards the root. The others end within three rotations at most."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "sibling red: 1 · black, black kids: 2 · near red: 3 · far red: 4"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ex",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
